 2. **Contact line** with a role-targeted relocation parenthetical when relevant: `Seattle, WA (open to <JD city>)`. The city comes from the JD location; never a blanket SF note (feedback_no_sf_location_on_cv).
 3. **`## Summary`**: 3 short paragraphs, each opening with a **bolded thesis sentence**: (a) identity claim tuned to the role family, (b) the Google years compressed with the role-relevant slice leading, (c) the newsroom decade as home-turf evidence.
 4. **`## Fit for <Role>, <Company>`** (comms/exec roles) or **`## Highlights`** (DevRel/technical roles) — THE key section, built from the JD's OWN requirement list: 6-8 bullets, each `- **<requirement paraphrase>:** <Mitchell evidence in 1-2 sentences>`. Tailoring lives here; if a JD requirement has no honest evidence, leave it out rather than stretch.
-5. **`## Experience`** — each role: `### <Title>` + `**<Company>** | <Period> | <Location>` meta line + a 1-line scope sentence, then **named-initiative sub-headers** as `#### <Initiative name (stack)>` (e.g. `#### Communications-triage agent (Apps Script + Gemini)`, `#### xGE Connects, peer-led technical workshop series`), each with a `- **Problem:** …` / `- **Action:** …` / `- **Impact:** …` triplet. No prose bullet walls.
+5. **`## Experience`** — each role: `### <Title>` + `**<Company>** | <Period> | <Location>` meta line + a 1-line scope sentence, then **named-initiative sub-headers** as `#### <Initiative name (stack)>` (e.g. `#### Communications-triage agent (Apps Script + Gemini)`, `#### xGE Connects, peer-led technical workshop series`), each with a `- **Problem:** …` / `- **Action:** …` / `- **Impact:** …` triplet. EVERY role with two or more substantive achievements MUST feature at least one such `####` Problem/Action/Impact block; a role of only flat bullets while other roles use P/A/I is a defect (supporting achievements may stay flat bullets after the featured block). No prose bullet walls. (feedback_cv_generation_conventions Rule B)
+5b. **Acronym first-reference context** — the FIRST time any non-obvious org or brand acronym appears anywhere in the CV (AJ+, xGE, TechStop, CGTN), expand it with a short context gloss on first use (e.g. `AJ+ (Al Jazeera's social media and viral-video output)`), then use the bare acronym every time after, including section headers. (feedback_cv_generation_conventions Rule A)
 6. **`## Earlier Career: Live National News (2010 – 2018)`** placed INSIDE the Experience section (the renderer treats a non-standard H2 there as a compressed group): a **bolded bridge line** first ("**The engine of live news is the engine of <role family>:** …" [cv.md:L44]), then one bullet per outlet.
 7. **`## Projects`** — placement flexes by role: DevRel/technical roles put Projects ABOVE Experience (the renderer honors source order); comms/exec roles put Projects after. Include career-ops [cv.md:L56-58], voice-os and tax-verification-agent [cv.md:L60-62]; add #FreeAhmed for comms/editorial roles [cv.md:L64-66].
 8. **`## Education`**, then **`## Certifications`** as one line (`AI Fluency · Claude 101 · Agent Skills · Model Context Protocol · Skill Builder (Opus cohort) | Anthropic | 2026`), then **`## Skills`** in 3 role-tuned `**Category:** items` lines.
